#exception-box(title: "THE SEVEN FATAL CUET TRAPS")[
  1. *Trap 1 (ASEAN Institutional Nature):* Assuming ASEAN has a supranational parliament or common currency like the EU. ASEAN has *no supranational government*; it operates strictly on informal consensus (*the 'ASEAN Way'*).
  2. *Trap 2 (Chinese Reform Pace):* Believing China adopted IMF Shock Therapy. China adopted a *gradual, phased transition* (agriculture in 1982, industry in 1998), preserving the party-state.
  3. *Trap 3 (ASEAN Founding Members):* Believing Vietnam was a founding member. Vietnam joined in *1995*; original 5 were Indonesia, Malaysia, Philippines, Singapore, Thailand.
  4. *Trap 4 (EU Common Constitution Status):* Believing the EU has an enacted federal constitution. The proposed Constitution was *rejected by French and Dutch voters in 2005* and was never ratified.
  5. *Trap 5 (Euro Launch Date vs Circulation Date):* The Euro was created in *1999* for accounting/financial markets, but physical cash entered public circulation on *1 January 2002*.
  6. *Trap 6 (Tibet Asylum Year):* The Dalai Lama escaped to India in *1959*, five years after the Panchsheel Agreement of 1954.
  7. *Trap 7 (Look East vs Act East):* 'Look East' was launched in *1991* by P.V. Narasimha Rao; 'Act East' was launched in *2014* by Narendra Modi.
]

