== Part 2: ASEAN Pillars, Chinese Reforms & Regional Security (Q6 to Q10)

#mcq(6, [The historic Treaty of Maastricht, which formally created the European Union and established the blueprint for the single currency (Euro), was signed in which year?], (
  [1992],
  [1989],
  [1995],
  [2002],
))
#solution(6, [The Maastricht Treaty:
- The *Maastricht Treaty* was signed on *7 February 1992* (entering into force on 1 November 1993), creating the European Union and establishing the Euro framework.
Therefore, Option A is the correct answer.], answer: [A])

#mcq(7, [Which Indian Prime Minister paid a historic breakthrough visit to Beijing in December 1988, marking the first visit by an Indian head of government in 34 years and restoring ties?], (
  [Indira Gandhi],
  [Rajiv Gandhi],
  [Atal Bihari Vajpayee],
  [P.V. Narasimha Rao],
))
#solution(7, [Rajiv Gandhi's 1988 China Visit:
- Prime Minister *Rajiv Gandhi* visited China in *December 1988*, meeting Deng Xiaoping.
- This historic visit thawed frozen relations, establishing joint working groups for border peace while expanding bilateral commerce.
Therefore, Option B is the correct answer.], answer: [B])

#mcq(8, [In which year did the People's Republic of China officially accede to the World Trade Organization (WTO), opening its massive manufacturing sector to global markets?], (
  [1991],
  [1998],
  [2001],
  [2008],
))
#solution(8, [China's Accession to the WTO:
- China formally joined the *World Trade Organization (WTO)* in *December 2001*, accelerating its integration into global supply chains as the "factory of the world".
Therefore, Option C is the correct answer.], answer: [C])

#mcq(9, [Which premier multilateral security forum was established by ASEAN in 1994 to facilitate dialogue on political and security issues among Asia-Pacific nations, including India and the US?], (
  [Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC)],
  [East Asia Summit (EAS)],
  [Shanghai Cooperation Organisation (SCO)],
  [ASEAN Regional Forum (ARF)],
))
#solution(9, [The ASEAN Regional Forum (ARF):
- The *ASEAN Regional Forum (ARF)* was founded in *1994* to foster constructive dialogue and consultation on political and security issues in the Asia-Pacific.
Therefore, Option D is the correct answer.], answer: [D])

#mcq(10, [What was the correct chronological sequence of phased economic privatization implemented by the Chinese government under Deng Xiaoping?], (
  [Privatization of heavy industry followed by privatization of agriculture],
  [Privatization of agriculture (1982) followed by privatization of industry (1998)],
  [Simultaneous overnight privatization of all sectors under IMF guidance],
  [Privatization of financial banks followed by collectivization of agriculture],
))
#solution(10, [Chronology of Chinese Privatization:
- China privatized *agriculture first in 1982* under the Household Responsibility System.
- *Industry was privatized later in 1998*, avoiding the disastrous economic collapse seen under Soviet Shock Therapy.
Therefore, Option B is the correct answer.], answer: [B])

